# wasm-pack emits the binary and the glue here. SMA-634: ALL FIVE are committed, and
# `moon run paigasus-kernel-ts:generate-wasm` is their only writer. A console loads the committed
# copy, because pnpm links a `file:` dependency once, at install time, before any build task runs.
#
# NOTE: `wasm-pack build` CLEANS its --out-dir each run (it overwrites .gitignore with a bare `*`
# and DELETES package.json, even with --no-pack), so every task builds into a gitignored scratch
# dir and copies out of it: `paigasus-kernel-ts:generate-wasm` uses .wasmpack-regen-out, that
# project's `test` task uses .wasmpack-test-out (the fresh build the drift gate compares against),
# and prebuild.yml uses .wasmpack-release-out. The `build` task runs no wasm-pack at all since
# SMA-634, so the fourth name it used to own, `.wasmpack-out`, has NO writer left and its ignore
# entry is gone with it — a dead ignore rule would hide a stale directory of that name from
# `git status` for good. If you have one left from an older checkout, delete it.
# The committed package.json/.gitignore/glue (what the `@paigasus/wasm` file: link resolves) are
# never clobbered. See ts/packages/paigasus-kernel/moon.yml.
*.wasm
# ...except the committed binary. The leading slash anchors the negation at the crate root, so a
# same-named file in a future sub-directory stays ignored.
!/paigasus_wasm_bg.wasm
.wasmpack-test-out/
.wasmpack-release-out/
.wasmpack-regen-out/

# The release path's UPLOAD staging dir, and the one scratch dir here that is deliberately NOT
# dot-prefixed: `actions/upload-artifact` excludes hidden files by default, so a dot-prefixed path
# uploads NOTHING and fails the job with "No files were found" — measured on prebuild.yml's first
# run with the wasm build in it, after the build step had already reported success. prebuild.yml
# copies the glue and the CRATE-ROOT package.json here, then uploads this directory (SMA-579).
wasm-dist/
